  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Santosh vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 22 September, 2022 Author: Rajendra Kumar Verma Bench: Rajendra Kumar Verma 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Indore Crr No. 3676 of 2022 (Santosh Vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh Dated : 22-09-2022",
    "facts": "T he applicant has been convicted for offence under Section 7(1) read with Section 16(1)(A)(i) and Section 14-A read with Section 16(1-C) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 and sentenced to undergo 6 months S.I., 3 months S.I. with fine of Rs.1000/-, Rs.500/- with default stipulation.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant has submitted that the applicant is innocent and has been falsely implicated in the present crime. He further submits that the learned Courts below have not followed Rule 14 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules, 1955, which is mandatory and has convicted the accused/applicant.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant has submitted that the applicant is innocent and has been falsely implicated in the present crime. He further submits that the learned Courts below have not followed Rule 14 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules, 1955, which is mandatory and has convicted the accused/applicant.",
